    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d284">

                <pb facs="0740" n="650" sameAs="frus:frus1875v01/pg650"/>

                <head>No. 280.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Edward
                            Thornton to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-01-23"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 23, 1875</date>.
                        (Received January 25.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of yesterday’s date, informing me of the views of the Government of
                    the United States relative to the extent of maritime jurisdiction which can
                    properly be claimed by any power.</p>
                <p>In thanking you for your note, I beg to say that I shall forward a copy of it to
                    the Earl of Derby by the first opportunity.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>EDW’D THORNTON.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
